@moonaan/picomatch 4.0.8-moonaan.1
Moonaan patch of picomatch 4.0.7 for CVE-2026-112366 / GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf.
Delete this fork once upstream releases a fixed version.

picomatch is Copyright (c) 2017-present, Jon Schlinkert, released under the
MIT License (see LICENSE). This package is unchanged from upstream tag 4.0.7
except:

- lib/parse.js + test/options.maxExtglobRecursion.js: upstream PR
  micromatch/picomatch#237 by Eduardo Seibt (head 1bf0d04563cb9ce568cf36efc5f6b7187d9911d5),
  which collapses single-branch repeated extglobs that contain a star
  (`+(P)` -> `(P)`, `*(P)` -> `(P)?`) so they no longer nest unbounded quantifiers.
- lib/parse.js (Moonaan): the collapse is skipped, keeping 4.0.7's output,
  when the branch has an escaped `/`, a `"` quote, a bracket that can match
  `/` (a literal `/`, [:punct:]/[:graph:]/[:print:]/[:ascii:], or a range
  spanning `/`), or when `regex: true`. Without this, #237 changed match
  results for e.g. `+(*\/)`, `+("*")`, `+([ab]*c)` with regex:true and
  `+(*[/])`. A generated differential against 4.0.7 (14,440 patterns x 2,801
  subjects x 5 option sets, 202M checks) shows 0 mismatches.
- test/moonaan.cve-2026-112366.js: timing regression test and the
  match-preservation cases above.
- package.json: renamed to @moonaan/picomatch, version 4.0.8-moonaan.1,
  published to GitHub Packages. The version sorts above 4.0.7 (so it is outside
  the advisory's `<= 4.0.7` range) and below a real 4.0.8.

Upstream PR #194 (named in the advisory) was evaluated and NOT used: it does not
bound `+(*)` / `+(*a)`.

Known residuals of this patch (all unchanged from 4.0.7, which is also
exponential on them). Do not compile untrusted glob patterns:
- Multi-alternative repeated extglobs with a starred branch, e.g. `+(*a|*b)`,
  `+(*a|b)` or `*(*.js|*.ts)`.
- Single-branch bodies the collapse deliberately skips because collapsing would
  change results: a bracket that can match `/` other than a bare `[/]`, e.g.
  `+(*[[:punct:]])` or `+(*[.-0])`.
